We are pleased to announce the Safaricom Discover Trainee Program in line with our future business needs.
Safaricom PLC is a leading Kenyan communications company and a leading digital innovator providing a wide range of communication services, including mobile voice, messaging, data, financial and converged services with a vision to empower a connected society. With the rapidly changing technology, it is critical to hire candidates with digital skills who can quickly adopt to the constant changes in the industry.
The program ensures that we continuously build a strong pool of talent who will lead our business in delivering our future growth ambitions.
The 18-month program is designed to prepare future leaders to take up challenging responsibilities and prepare them for business leadership roles. The program encompasses rotations within and across functions in an accelerated learning environment with continuous coaching and mentorship programs.
We are looking for bright and well-rounded digital leaders, with strong agile team working and leadership competencies.
Key accountabilities and decision ownership:
Take responsibility for and commit to continuous self-development throughout the program in order to achieve a high level of competence as outlined by the program specifications;
Observe all Safaricom policies, procedures and demonstrate Safaricom Way behaviors and values;
Adapt to different working environments, teams and cultures;
Make sound, effective and timely decisions within the program scope;
Be positive, courageous and seek opportunities to learn and develop;
Inspire and influence others;
Work with the assigned coach to perform and exceed set expectations;
Attend and pass all core training prerequisites and programs within the specified time-frames;
Successfully manage and complete all assigned projects and assessments as per program requirements and schedule;
Commit to be available to work in any part of the business during the program and be placed in any department within the business aligned to the GMP;
Work with the assigned Coach to identify innovations and business improvement opportunities;
Willingly and continuously share knowledge and learning with program peers as well as coaches
Accurately maintain and update a personal portfolio of all learning received.
QUALIFICATIONS
You must have graduated with a Diploma/Degree in the past 1 year or awaiting graduation in the next 6 months.
Knowledge and experience in any of these Digital skills (Digital Marketing, data analytics, Robotics, Automation, Artificial Intelligence, Cloud, Security, Agile, Lean, UI/UX, Digital Thinking, Digital Care, Digital Sales and any other related digital skills)
Innovation hungry, Ambitious and a team player;
A person who can work to deliver new solutions to the business
Tech Savvy and analytical;
Focused, flexible, engaging and collaborative;
Self-driven and clear demonstration of self-learning
Demonstrate Leadership Skills, creativity, critical thinking and versatility.

Qualifications
For appointment to this grade, an officer must have:-
A cumulative number of Fifteen (15) years relevant experience from the date of admission as an Advocate of the High Court of Kenya
OR
served for Two (2) years at the level of Assistant Director of Public Prosecutions DPP4/JG’Q’.
Bachelor of Laws (LLB) degree from a recognized university; Postgraduate Diploma in Legal Studies from the Council of Legal Education;
Admission as an Advocate of the High Court of Kenya;
Demonstrated merit and ability as reflected in work perfomance and results; and
Be a member of a recognized professional body.
Note
Possession of a Masters degree in law or any other social science from a recognized institution and a Strategic Leadership Development Programme lasting not less than six (6) weeks from a recognized institution will be an added advantage.
Core Skills/Competencies
In addition to the above requirements, an officer must have the following skills:-
Litigation and Prosecutorial skills;
Legislation and reform skills
Policy formulation and implementation skills;
Research skills;
Thorough understanding of national goals, policies and objectives and ability to relate them to proper management of prosecution services;
Knowledge of criminal justice system;
Knowledge of relevant legislation;
Knowledge of professional standards;
Leadership skills;
ICT skills;
Budgeting skills;
Analytical skills;
Resource management skills;
Interpersonal and communication skills.
Negotiation skills; and
Personal Qualities
In addition to the above requirements, an officer must have the following qualities:-
Ability to articulate, interpret and implement national and international policies and development goals;
Honesty and integrity
